From ebe0718d3dfc3ee1d17f485039f9d40e563aefc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 23:51:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00693/11171] [outer-loop] Blog publish gate: pre-push guard +
 draft-never-on-main rule

Fixes the 2026-06-05 gap where the conductor's milestone-close auto-push shipped
an un-approved blog draft to Pages before operator approval (main auto-deploys +
conductor auto-pushes main = the operator-only-publication rule could not hold).

#2 Mechanical guard (pre-push, covers the conductor's --no-verify auto-push):
  - scripts/blog_publish_guard.py: refuses pushing any docs/blog/*.html POST to
    main unless on the allowlist; index.html exempt; fail-open on git infra error,
    fail-closed on a confirmed unapproved post. Tested 4 ways (clean=allow,
    unapproved=block, allowlisted=allow, non-main branch=allow).
  - docs/blog/published-allowlist.txt: operator-approved post manifest (9 live).
  - .pre-commit-config.yaml: blog-publish-guard at stage pre-push; installed via
    `pre-commit install --hook-type pre-push`.

#1 Convention (documented): blog drafts live on a BRANCH, never on main; publish =
  operator adds the filename to the allowlist. ops/known-issues.md OPERATOR
  CONSTRAINTS + memory feedback_blog_draft_branch_not_main.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
